<!-- Exercise 031 - StaticAndDynamicResource (beginner).
     Goal:   Declare a shared resource and consume it from two TextBlocks -
             one through StaticResource, one through DynamicResource - so a
             runtime resource swap reaches only the DynamicResource consumer.
     Drills: ResourceDictionary, StaticResource vs DynamicResource.
     Passes: dotnet test, filtered to Ex031_ (see the exact command in
     Ex031_StaticAndDynamicResource.axaml.cs - an XML comment may not hold
     two hyphens in a row, so it cannot appear here). -->
<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Beginner.Ex031_StaticAndDynamicResource">
  <!-- TODO: replace this placeholder with:
         <UserControl.Resources>
           <x:Double x:Key="Size">17</x:Double>
         </UserControl.Resources>
         <StackPanel Spacing="8">
           <TextBlock Name="StaticText" Text="Static" FontSize="{StaticResource Size}" />
           <TextBlock Name="DynamicText" Text="Dynamic" FontSize="{DynamicResource Size}" />
         </StackPanel>
       Both start at FontSize 17. StaticResource resolves the value once, at
       load time; DynamicResource keeps a live subscription on the resource
       key. The test replaces Resources["Size"] afterwards - StaticText must
       stay at 17, DynamicText must follow to the new value. Setting
       FontSize="17" as a plain literal on both reproduces the starting
       numbers with no resource lookup at all and cannot follow the swap on
       either element - and swapping which markup extension goes on which
       named TextBlock also fails, because the test checks each name
       individually. -->
  <StackPanel>
    <TextBlock Text="TODO" />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
